Read-only views.

list defaults to takeable work — unclaimed and unblocked — computed from one
traversal plus the first three lines of each ticket. No bodies are read. -a
shows every open ticket with its state and, for blocked ones, what is
blocking them.

tree renders the hierarchy with closed tickets marked [x].

check validates the three structural lines, that every line before the first
blank is a declared field, that required fields are present, that every needs
entry resolves, that the needs graph is acyclic, that no number is issued
twice, that every number has a registry entry and every entry a ticket, that
no directory inside a ticket is anything but a number or c, that claims and
locks have living holders, and that both generated documents match what would
be generated now. It changes nothing and exits nonzero on findings.

Four shell faults found by running it, all recorded in the design.

check reported into a shell variable incremented inside pipelines, so the
subshells lost every increment and it exited 0 whatever it found. Findings go
to a file now.

tree sorted structural keys under the ambient locale, which ignores the / in
a path key and put children ahead of their own parents. Forced to LC_ALL=C.

survey emitted an empty field between tabs; tab is IFS whitespace, so read
collapsed two tabs into one and every later field shifted left, blanking
every title. It writes - for no blockers.

tree was recursive, and a recursive shell function cannot hold loop state —
the inner call clobbers the outer cursor, and per-function prefixes do not
help against a function colliding with itself. It sorts a precomputed key
instead.

Done: implemented in bin/pidly, covered by tests/views.sh (26 cases,
including that check leaves the tracker byte-identical).
